lynxpm (0.7.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * **Breaking: binary renamed from `lynx` to `lynxpm`.** The `lynx`
    name collides with the widely-packaged text-mode web browser on
    Debian/Ubuntu, so the CLI now installs at `/usr/bin/lynxpm`.
    Replace any `lynx` invocation with `lynxpm` in scripts, cron
    entries, and Lynxfile tooling.
  * package: Debian package renamed from `lynx-pm` to `lynxpm`.
    Drop the incorrect `Conflicts/Replaces/Provides: lynx` clauses
    that were attempting to override the real `lynx` browser package.
  * systemd: user-mode unit renamed to `lynxd.service`. Manage with
    `systemctl --user enable --now lynxd`. System mode unchanged.
  * release artifacts: `lynx_linux_*` -> `lynxpm_linux_*` (binaries,
    signatures, SBOMs). `.deb` name is `lynxpm_<ver>_<arch>.deb`.

